# GitHub release binaries to install when not already in PATH.
# Copy this file to ~/.config/untapped/conf and edit — no script changes needed.
#
# Format: name | github_repo | asset_pattern | binary_in_archive | os_filter | arch_filter | version_pin
#
# Placeholders in asset_pattern:
#   {VERSION} — release tag, v-prefix stripped (latest, or version_pin if set)
#   {OS}      — darwin or linux
#   {ARCH}    — arm64 or amd64
#
# os_filter / arch_filter: omit (or leave empty) to match any.
# Mismatched entries are skipped (with a reason in the exit summary)
# before anything is downloaded.
#
# version_pin (optional): pin a release tag (e.g. v1.2.3). Install/upgrade
# use that tag instead of the latest; leave empty for latest.
#
# binary_in_archive matching *.app/Contents/MacOS/* is treated as a macOS app
# bundle: the whole bundle is preserved under ~/.local/opt/<name> and
# symlinked into ~/.local/bin — required for entitlement-gated tools
# (Virtualization/Hypervisor, etc.), which get SIGKILLed if the binary is
# flattened out of the bundle (confirmed with tart).
#
# Examples — four common shapes:

# Flat archive, OS+arch in the filename:
usql    | xo/usql        | usql-{VERSION}-{OS}-{ARCH}.tar.bz2 | usql                         |        |

# macOS .app bundle (entitlement-preserving install):
tart    | openai/tart    | tart.tar.gz                        | tart.app/Contents/MacOS/tart | darwin |

# Fixed asset name, macOS-only (no {OS}/{ARCH} in the name):
softnet | openai/softnet | softnet.tar.gz                     | softnet                      | darwin |

# Bare AppImage, Linux x86_64 only (arch token not in every asset name):
shotcut | mltframework/shotcut | shotcut-linux-x86_64-{VERSION}.AppImage | shotcut | linux | amd64
